{Sentence 1: "The color gamut of a monitor is enclosed by the primary colors of the device on the chromaticity diagram."}
{Sentence 2: "The color gamut of a device is defined as the range of colors which it can produce or record."}
{Sentence 3: "The color gamut of a device is usually shown by an enclosed area of the primary colors of the device on the chromaticity diagram."}
{Sentence 4: "The color gamut of a device is a collection of colors, and it is logical that it can also be described using hue, saturation, and brightness."}
{Sentence 5: "The color gamut of a device is represented on a chromaticity diagram, with the missing dimension being brightness, which is perpendicular to the screen or sheet of paper."}

